      "input_state": "elemental Al, Ti, Zr, Nb, Ta",
      "output_state": "as-cast ingot",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "page": 2,
          "section": "2.1 Material Preparation",
          "quote": "The AlTiZrNbTa alloy was prepared via vacuum arc melting. Due to the difference in melting points between Al and refractory metals, Al tends to volatilize during the melting process, potentially leading to deviations from the target alloy composition. To mitigate this, a two-step melting process was used in this study. Firstly, high-purity Al (99.99 wt.%) and Ti (99.99 wt.%) were melted together in a predetermined ratio to create an AlTi intermediate alloy. subsequently, this intermediate alloy was remelted with high-purity Zr, Ni, and Ta ( ‡ 99.99 wt.%) in the vacuum arc furnace to synthesize the initial alloy ingot. During melting, the furnace pressure was kept below 5 9 10 -3 Pa and high-purity argon gas was employed as a protective atmosphere to minimize oxidation and further volatilization. The ingot was repeatedly melted ﬁve times. The ﬁnal AlTiZrNbTa alloy was a bowl-shaped ingot approximately 30 mm high and 40 mm in diameter.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "d0da00c9b35e3a23:part:001"
        },
        {
          "page": 9,
          "section": "4. Conclusions",
          "quote": "In this study, the AlTiZrNbTa RHEA was prepared via vacuum arc melting.",
          "table": null,
          "figure": null,
          "chunk_id": "d0da00c9b35e3a23:part:002"
